  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale\n   This approach uses a genetic algorithm tailored for non-negative functions with bounded integrals. Unlike the previous gradient-based optimization, this method explores a broader solution space by handling the objective function directly through tournament selection and controlled mutation. The key bottleneck addressed is the gradient-based optimization's tendency to get stuck in local minima, which we overcome by using a population-based search. We maintain solution diversity while ensuring constraints are met through projection. The implementation uses a scheduled crossover and mutation, with adaptive resolution increases if time permits.\n\n2. Mathematical specification\n   - Variables: Real-valued vector h \u2208 \u211d\u207f representing the step function, with n = n_points.\n   - Constraints:\n     - Integration constraint: \u222bh(x)dx = 1 \u2192 \u2211h[i] \u00b7 dx = 1 \u2192 \u2211h = k (with dx = 2/n, k = n/2)\n     - Boundedness: 0 \u2264 h[i] \u2264 1 for all i\n   - Objective: Minimize max\u2096 [\u222bh(x)(1-h(x+k))dx] = max\u2096 [correlation(h, 1-h) \u00b7 dx] (mode='full')}\n\n3. Implementation procedure\n   a. Initialization:\n      i. If initial_h_values provided, use as primary candidate; otherwise generate random projections\n   b. Genetic Algorithm Setup:\n      i. Population size: 48 (reserve 2 for potential crossover)\n      ii. Tournament selection with replacement every generation\n      iii. Crossover rate: 0.7 (one-point crossover followed by projection)\n      iv. Mutation rate: 0.3 (slight perturbations)\n      v. Generations: 100\u2013200 (limited by budget)\n   c. GA Update Loop:\n      i. Evaluate fitness (negative C5) for every candidate\n      ii. Elitism: keep best 10% of population\n      iii. Selection: tourney_size=5\n      iv. Crossover: single-point followed by projection\n      v. Mutation: additive normal noise followed by projection\n   d. Resolution handling:\n      i. Base resolution: 200 points (slightly higher than parent's 180)\n      ii. Multiplier: [1.0, 1.2, 1.4, 1.6, 1.8, 2.0]\n      iii. Increase when remaining time > 300 seconds\n   e. Post-GA polish:\n      i. Single SLSQP call with projected gradients\n      ii. Resolution increase if budget allows\n   f. Validity check: After every step, enforce projection\n\n4. Search choices and variations\n   a. Base config:\n      - Initial population: 48 projected candidates\n      - Crossover point: Central point between parents\n      - Mutation noise: \u03c3 = 0.02\n   b. Adaptive adjustments:\n      i. Increase mutation rate if stuck in convergence\n      ii. Reduce crossover rate after population diversity drops\n      iii. Switch between density-preserving and amplitude-preserving mutation based on problem difficulty\n\n5. Compute budget and robustness\n   a. Cost estimate:\n      - Correlation: O(n\u00b2) operations (\u224820ms for n=200)\n      - Projection: 80 iterations per candidate (\u22480.1ms)\n      - GA per generation: 48 candidates\n   b. Time allocations:\n      - GA main phase: 3,000 seconds (fixed population) or 1,300 seconds (budget-based)\n      - Post-GA polishing: 100 seconds\n      - Resolution increase: 200 seconds\n   c. Deadline handling: Abort GA after 10 unchanged generations\n   d. Budget exceedance: Return best candidate without resolution increase\n   e. Numerical robustness:\n      - Precision: 1e-10 tolerance for projections\n      - Omit negative/nan fitness values from selection\n\n6. Validation and return contract\n   a. Feasibility checks:\n      - Confirm each candidate satisfies: 0 \u2264 h[i] \u2264 1 and \u2211h = target_sum\n      - Reject invalid candidates for the current generation\n   b. Objective consistency:\n      - Recompute C5 before final return using same code\n      - Include small Lipschitz check: |\u2207C5| should \u2248 correlation magnitude\n   c. Early termination:\n      - Return if no improvement for 50 generations\n      - Max generations: 200\n   d. Implementation signature:\n        def run(*args, **kwargs):\n            initialize_population()\n            while time_remaining():\n                perform_ga_generation()\n            polish_solution()\n            return final_candidate, final_c5, n_points",
